From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:38:22 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: remove the integrated PHY firmware loader and its MDIO
 bus

Both are the switch driver's work now. It stages the firmware for the
integrated PHYs out of the device tree node that names it, releases each
PHY from reset through the reset framework rather than through hardcoded
bits, and registers the management bus itself, in the order the hardware
wants and without the second driver that used to wait on the first.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/Makefile b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/Makefile
index 60061230f5f6..7ef86ecf1aea 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/Makefile
@@ -18,21 +18,6 @@ intel-xrx500-gswip-y += cqm/grx500/cbm_ports.o
 intel-xrx500-gswip-y += dma/hdma.o
 intel-xrx500-gswip-y += tmu/tmu_init.o tmu/drv_tmu_ll.o
 
-#
-# The GPHY firmware is proprietary and lives in the rootfs, so the loader
-# is kept out of the kernel image and gets a module of its own.
-#
-obj-$(CONFIG_INTEL_XRX500_MDIO) += intel-xrx500-mdio.o
-
-intel-xrx500-mdio-y := xrx500_phy_fw.o
-
-#
-# The MDIO bus driver consumes xrx500_gphy_fw_is_loaded(), so it ships in
-# the same module as xrx500_phy_fw.o and that call stays intra-module.
-# Without the bus, phylink_of_phy_connect() has no PHY to find.
-#
-intel-xrx500-mdio-y += switch-api/mdio_xrx500.o
-
 #
 # The buffer-manager conduit netdev. Built in, never a module: its transmit
 # path calls MIPS cache maintenance which is not exported to modules.
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/include/xrx500_phy_fw.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/include/xrx500_phy_fw.h
deleted file mode 100644
index 8abeeecc47e6..000000000000
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/include/xrx500_phy_fw.h
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,36 +0,0 @@
-/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
-/*
